data: {"item":{"encrypted_content":"We need to implement task 001 correctly. The previous submission failed test \"blank project input is rejected\": expected alert with role='alert' containing text \"Project name is required\". Likely the UI didn't create an alert element with appropriate role. Need to implement front-end to show alert visible (maybe \u003cdiv role=\"alert\"\u003e). Also need to ensure blank or whitespace-only name triggers alert and does not add project row.\n\nWe must use Node.js 22.22.1, ES modules, built-in http and sqlite. No external dependencies. Use npm start script to run server.\n\nWe need to implement server with SQLite DB storing projects (id integer primary key autoincrement, name text). Serve static HTML/JS/CSS. Provide endpoints for creating project (POST /projects), listing projects (GET /api/projects maybe). For simplicity, can embed JS in HTML that uses fetch to backend.\n\nRouting: For root '/', serve index.html with list and creation form.\n\nFor /projects/:id, serve project.html showing project name heading and button back to '/'. The server can serve same HTML with dynamic injection using server-side rendering (simple templating) or client fetch.\n\nSimpler: Use client-side JS to fetch project details via API.\n\nDefine API endpoints:\n\n- GET /api/projects -\u003e list\n- POST /api/projects (JSON {name}) -\u003e create, returns created project {id, name}\n- GET /api/projects/:id -\u003e get single\n\nNeed to serve /health.\n\nImplementation constraints: No external dependencies, so cannot use express; use node:http.\n\nAlso need to serve static files from a directory (public). Use fs to read.\n\nImplement server.js with:\n\nimport http, { createServer } from 'node:http';\nimport { readFile } from 'node:fs/promises';\nimport path from 'node:path';\nimport { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\nimport sqlite3 from 'node:sqlite';\nimport sqlite3Driver from 'node:sqlite3';\n\nInitialize DB with file path from env DB_PATH or default to './workboard.db'.\n\nCreate table if not exists projects (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT, name TEXT NOT NULL).\n\nHandle request URL and method.\n\n- If pathname starts with '/api/projects':\n   - If method GET and no id: return JSON list.\n   - If method GET with id: return project.\n   - If method POST: parse JSON body, trim name, if empty respond 400 with message; else insert and respond 201 with project JSON.\n\n- If pathname === '/health': respond 200 JSON.\n\n- For other GET requests, serve static files from public directory, default to index.html for '/' and for any path not starting with /api/.\n\nSet headers CORS maybe not needed.\n\nNow front-end.\n\npublic/index.html:\n\n\u003c!DOCTYPE html\u003e\n\u003chtml lang=\"en\"\u003e\n\u003chead\u003e\n\u003cmeta charset=\"UTF-8\"\u003e\n\u003ctitle\u003eWorkboard\u003c/title\u003e\n\u003c/head\u003e\n\u003cbody\u003e\n\u003ch1\u003eWorkboard\u003c/h1\u003e\n\u003clabel for=\"project-name\"\u003eProject name\u003c/label\u003e\n\u003cinput type=\"text\" id=\"project-name\" aria-label=\"Project name\"\u003e\n\u003cbutton id=\"create-project\"\u003eCreate project\u003c/button\u003e\n\u003cdiv id=\"alert\" role=\"alert\" style=\"color:red;display:none;\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cul id=\"project-list\"\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cscript type=\"module\" src=\"index.js\"\u003e\u003c/script\u003e\n\u003c/body\u003e\n\u003c/html\u003e\n\npublic/index.js:\n\nimport { fetchProjects, createProject } from './api.js';\n\nfunction showAlert(message) {\n  const alertDiv = document.getElementById('alert');\n  alertDiv.textContent = message;\n  alertDiv.style.display = 'block';\n}\nfunction hideAlert() {\n  const alertDiv = document.getElementById('alert');\n  alertDiv.style.display = 'none';\n}\nasync function loadProjects() {\n  const list = document.getElementById('project-list');\n  list.innerHTML = '';\n  const projects = await fetchProjects();\n  for (const p of projects) {\n    const li = document.createElement('li');\n    li.dataset.testid = 'project-row';\n    li.textContent = p.name + ' ';\n    const btn = document.createElement('button');\n    btn.textContent = 'Open project';\n    btn.addEventListener('click', () =\u003e {\n      location.href = `/projects/${p.id}`;\n    });\n    li.appendChild(btn);\n    list.appendChild(li);\n  }\n}\ndocument.getElementById('create-project').addEventListener('click', async () =\u003e {\n  hideAlert();\n  const input = document.getElementById('project-name');\n  const name = input.value.trim();\n  if (!name) {\n    showAlert('Project name is required');\n    return;\n  }\n  try {\n    await createProject(name);\n    input.value = '';\n    await loadProjects();\n  } catch (e) {\n    showAlert(e.message);\n  }\n});\nloadProjects();\n\npublic/api.js:\n\nexport async function fetchProjects() {\n  const res = await fetch('/api/projects');\n  if (!res.ok) throw new Error('Failed to fetch projects');\n  return await res.json();\n}\nexport async function createProject(name) {\n  const res = await fetch('/api/projects', {\n    method: 'POST',\n    headers: {'Content-Type': 'application/json'},\n    body: JSON.stringify({name})\n  });\n  if (!res.ok) {\n    const data = await res.json().catch(()=\u003e({}));\n    const msg = data.error || 'Failed to create project';\n    throw new Error(msg);\n  }\n  return await res.json();\n}\nexport async function fetchProject(id) {\n  const res = await fetch(`/api/projects/${id}`);\n  if (!res.ok) throw new Error('Project not found');\n  return await res.json();\n}\n\npublic/project.html:\n\n\u003c!DOCTYPE html\u003e\n\u003chtml lang=\"en\"\u003e\n\u003chead\u003e\n\u003cmeta charset=\"UTF-8\"\u003e\n\u003ctitle\u003eProject\u003c/title\u003e\n\u003c/head\u003e\n\u003cbody\u003e\n\u003ch1 id=\"project-name\"\u003e\u003c/h1\u003e\n\u003cbutton id=\"back\"\u003eProjects\u003c/button\u003e\n\u003cscript type=\"module\"\u003e\nimport { fetchProject } from './api.js';\nconst id = location.pathname.split('/').pop();\nfetchProject(id).then(p =\u003e {\n  document.getElementById('project-name').textContent = p.name;\n});\ndocument.getElementById('back').addEventListener('click', () =\u003e {\n  location.href = '/';\n});\n\u003c/script\u003e\n\u003c/body\u003e\n\u003c/html\u003e\n\nNeed to serve these static files.\n\nAlso ensure data-testid attribute: In li we set data-testid=\"project-row\". In test they probably use getByTestId('project-row') to count rows. Provide that.\n\nAlso need to ensure alert role='alert' and visible when blank input.\n\nImplementation details for server static:\n\nfunction serveStatic(filePath) { readFile(filePath) ... content-type based on extension.\n\nMap '/' -\u003e '/public/index.html', '/projects/:id' -\u003e '/public/project.html', others as static.\n\nSet default DB_PATH env var fallback.\n\nAdd npm scripts: start: \"node server.js\". Need package.json.\n\nLet's check repository current state.","id":"rs_822792","summary":[{"text":"We need to implement task 001 correctly. The previous submission failed test \"blank project input is rejected\": expected alert with role='alert' containing text \"Project name is required\". Likely the UI didn't create an alert element with appropriate role. Need to implement front-end to show alert visible (maybe \u003cdiv role=\"alert\"\u003e). Also need to ensure blank or whitespace-only name triggers alert and does not add project row.\n\nWe must use Node.js 22.22.1, ES modules, built-in http and sqlite. No external dependencies. Use npm start script to run server.\n\nWe need to implement server with SQLite DB storing projects (id integer primary key autoincrement, name text). Serve static HTML/JS/CSS. Provide endpoints for creating project (POST /projects), listing projects (GET /api/projects maybe). For simplicity, can embed JS in HTML that uses fetch to backend.\n\nRouting: For root '/', serve index.html with list and creation form.\n\nFor /projects/:id, serve project.html showing project name heading and button back to '/'. The server can serve same HTML with dynamic injection using server-side rendering (simple templating) or client fetch.\n\nSimpler: Use client-side JS to fetch project details via API.\n\nDefine API endpoints:\n\n- GET /api/projects -\u003e list\n- POST /api/projects (JSON {name}) -\u003e create, returns created project {id, name}\n- GET /api/projects/:id -\u003e get single\n\nNeed to serve /health.\n\nImplementation constraints: No external dependencies, so cannot use express; use node:http.\n\nAlso need to serve static files from a directory (public). Use fs to read.\n\nImplement server.js with:\n\nimport http, { createServer } from 'node:http';\nimport { readFile } from 'node:fs/promises';\nimport path from 'node:path';\nimport { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\nimport sqlite3 from 'node:sqlite';\nimport sqlite3Driver from 'node:sqlite3';\n\nInitialize DB with file path from env DB_PATH or default to './workboard.db'.\n\nCreate table if not exists projects (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT, name TEXT NOT NULL).\n\nHandle request URL and method.\n\n- If pathname starts with '/api/projects':\n   - If method GET and no id: return JSON list.\n   - If method GET with id: return project.\n   - If method POST: parse JSON body, trim name, if empty respond 400 with message; else insert and respond 201 with project JSON.\n\n- If pathname === '/health': respond 200 JSON.\n\n- For other GET requests, serve static files from public directory, default to index.html for '/' and for any path not starting with /api/.\n\nSet headers CORS maybe not needed.\n\nNow front-end.\n\npublic/index.html:\n\n\u003c!DOCTYPE html\u003e\n\u003chtml lang=\"en\"\u003e\n\u003chead\u003e\n\u003cmeta charset=\"UTF-8\"\u003e\n\u003ctitle\u003eWorkboard\u003c/title\u003e\n\u003c/head\u003e\n\u003cbody\u003e\n\u003ch1\u003eWorkboard\u003c/h1\u003e\n\u003clabel for=\"project-name\"\u003eProject name\u003c/label\u003e\n\u003cinput type=\"text\" id=\"project-name\" aria-label=\"Project name\"\u003e\n\u003cbutton id=\"create-project\"\u003eCreate project\u003c/button\u003e\n\u003cdiv id=\"alert\" role=\"alert\" style=\"color:red;display:none;\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cul id=\"project-list\"\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cscript type=\"module\" src=\"index.js\"\u003e\u003c/script\u003e\n\u003c/body\u003e\n\u003c/html\u003e\n\npublic/index.js:\n\nimport { fetchProjects, createProject } from './api.js';\n\nfunction showAlert(message) {\n  const alertDiv = document.getElementById('alert');\n  alertDiv.textContent = message;\n  alertDiv.style.display = 'block';\n}\nfunction hideAlert() {\n  const alertDiv = document.getElementById('alert');\n  alertDiv.style.display = 'none';\n}\nasync function loadProjects() {\n  const list = document.getElementById('project-list');\n  list.innerHTML = '';\n  const projects = await fetchProjects();\n  for (const p of projects) {\n    const li = document.createElement('li');\n    li.dataset.testid = 'project-row';\n    li.textContent = p.name + ' ';\n    const btn = document.createElement('button');\n    btn.textContent = 'Open project';\n    btn.addEventListener('click', () =\u003e {\n      location.href = `/projects/${p.id}`;\n    });\n    li.appendChild(btn);\n    list.appendChild(li);\n  }\n}\ndocument.getElementById('create-project').addEventListener('click', async () =\u003e {\n  hideAlert();\n  const input = document.getElementById('project-name');\n  const name = input.value.trim();\n  if (!name) {\n    showAlert('Project name is required');\n    return;\n  }\n  try {\n    await createProject(name);\n    input.value = '';\n    await loadProjects();\n  } catch (e) {\n    showAlert(e.message);\n  }\n});\nloadProjects();\n\npublic/api.js:\n\nexport async function fetchProjects() {\n  const res = await fetch('/api/projects');\n  if (!res.ok) throw new Error('Failed to fetch projects');\n  return await res.json();\n}\nexport async function createProject(name) {\n  const res = await fetch('/api/projects', {\n    method: 'POST',\n    headers: {'Content-Type': 'application/json'},\n    body: JSON.stringify({name})\n  });\n  if (!res.ok) {\n    const data = await res.json().catch(()=\u003e({}));\n    const msg = data.error || 'Failed to create project';\n    throw new Error(msg);\n  }\n  return await res.json();\n}\nexport async function fetchProject(id) {\n  const res = await fetch(`/api/projects/${id}`);\n  if (!res.ok) throw new Error('Project not found');\n  return await res.json();\n}\n\npublic/project.html:\n\n\u003c!DOCTYPE html\u003e\n\u003chtml lang=\"en\"\u003e\n\u003chead\u003e\n\u003cmeta charset=\"UTF-8\"\u003e\n\u003ctitle\u003eProject\u003c/title\u003e\n\u003c/head\u003e\n\u003cbody\u003e\n\u003ch1 id=\"project-name\"\u003e\u003c/h1\u003e\n\u003cbutton id=\"back\"\u003eProjects\u003c/button\u003e\n\u003cscript type=\"module\"\u003e\nimport { fetchProject } from './api.js';\nconst id = location.pathname.split('/').pop();\nfetchProject(id).then(p =\u003e {\n  document.getElementById('project-name').textContent = p.name;\n});\ndocument.getElementById('back').addEventListener('click', () =\u003e {\n  location.href = '/';\n});\n\u003c/script\u003e\n\u003c/body\u003e\n\u003c/html\u003e\n\nNeed to serve these static files.\n\nAlso ensure data-testid attribute: In li we set data-testid=\"project-row\". In test they probably use getByTestId('project-row') to count rows. Provide that.\n\nAlso need to ensure alert role='alert' and visible when blank input.\n\nImplementation details for server static:\n\nfunction serveStatic(filePath) { readFile(filePath) ... content-type based on extension.\n\nMap '/' -\u003e '/public/index.html', '/projects/:id' -\u003e '/public/project.html', others as static.\n\nSet default DB_PATH env var fallback.\n\nAdd npm scripts: start: \"node server.js\". Need package.json.\n\nLet's check repository current state.","type":"summary_text"}],"type":"reasoning"},"output_index":0,"sequence_number":1452,"type":"response.output_item.done"}

